# Architecture conventions

Atlas OS is a modular monolith: one Next.js 16 App Router application with
strict internal boundaries. No microservices. See `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Layout

```
src/app/            routes only: thin, compose modules, no business logic
src/core/           infrastructure: env, db, auth, ai, crypto, events, jobs, observability
src/modules/<name>/ domain (pure), server (data + use cases), ui (components)
src/design/         design system: tokens, primitives, shell, motion
```

Modules in Phase 1: `identity`, `conversations`, `memory`, `ventures`,
`intelligence`.

## Dependency rules

- `app` → `modules`, `design`, `core`
- `modules/*/ui` → own `domain`, `design`, other modules' public `index.ts` only
- `modules/*/server` → own `domain`, `core`, other modules' public `index.ts`
- `modules/*/domain` → nothing except `zod` and shared types (pure, testable)
- `core` → never imports from `modules` or `app`
- Provider SDKs (`@ai-sdk/*`, `better-auth`, `postgres`) are imported only in
  `src/core`.

## AI

- All model access goes through `src/core/ai/model-router.ts` using roles
  (`atlas.primary`, `atlas.fast`, `atlas.embed`, `atlas.extract`). Roles map
  to provider models in one config file. Modules never name a vendor model.
- Atlas orchestration uses AI SDK 7 (`streamText` / `ToolLoopAgent`,
  `instructions`, `isStepCount`, `toolApproval`, `onEnd`). Tools are defined
  with `tool({ inputSchema })` and registered through the capability registry
  in `src/modules/intelligence/server/capabilities`.
- Context assembly (profile, memories, active ventures/projects, conversation
  history) is a pure function in `src/modules/intelligence/domain` that
  returns a typed `AtlasContext`; the prompt builder renders it.
- Memory writes happen after the response via `after()` (Phase 1) behind the
  `JobRunner` port in `src/core/jobs` so a durable engine can replace it.

## Data

- Drizzle schema per module in `src/modules/<name>/server/schema.ts`,
  aggregated in `src/core/db/schema.ts`. Migrations in `drizzle/` are
  generated, reviewed, and committed. Enable extensions (`vector`) in a
  hand-written first migration.
- Every user-owned table has `user_id` and every query filters by the
  authenticated user id. There is no shared/global data in Phase 1.
- Store `UIMessage.parts` as JSONB; convert with `convertToModelMessages`
  at call time. Never store provider-specific message formats.
- Emit an `atlas_event` row for significant domain events (conversation
  created, memory created/superseded, project status changed, tool executed).
  This is the audit spine and the future trigger surface for Operatives.

## Server entry points

- Every page, route handler, and server action calls `requireSession()` from
  `src/core/auth/server.ts`. `proxy.ts` only does optimistic cookie checks.
- Validate all inputs with Zod. Return typed errors; never leak stack traces.
- Route handlers for streaming live under `src/app/api/atlas/*`.
